  "question": {
    "text": "Angle between the planes $x+y+2 z=6$ and $2 x-y+z=9$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "68s8W",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Tk0QQ",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "nfdMX",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yemkS",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Equations of planes are\r\n$x+y+2 z-6=0$\r\nand $\\quad 2 x-y+z-9=0$\r\n$\\cos \\theta=\\frac{a_{1} a_{2}+b_{1}b_{2}+c\r\n_{1}c_{2}}{\\sqrt{a_{1}^{2}+b_{1}^{2}+c_{1}^{2}} \\sqrt{a_{2}^{2}+b_{2}^{2}+c_{2}^{2}}}$\r\n$=\\frac{1 \\times 2+1 \\times(-1)+2 \\times 1}{\\sqrt{1+1+4} \\sqrt{4+1+1}}$\r\n$=\\frac{2-1+2}{\\sqrt{6} \\times \\sqrt{6}}=\\frac{3}{6}=\\frac{1}{2}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\cos \\theta=\\cos \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$",
    "image": null
  },
